    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `fill_gaps` in `app/gaps.py`. The existing tests pass (2 of 2), and a manual check on an edge-case frame gave the correct results.\n\n**How it works:** it copies the frame, then groups `temp_c` by station. Each missing value takes the station's most recent earlier temperature, or its first later one if there's no earlier one. Temperatures that were already there are never changed, and the other columns are left as they are.\n\n**What the check covered:**\n- Stations interleaved with each other.\n- A station whose first report has no temperature, which correctly took that station's first later value.\n- A station with no temperatures at all, which kept its missing values.\n- Repeated index labels, which didn't cause any misalignment.\n- The input frame is unchanged afterwards.\n\n**Decision for you:** a row with no station at all keeps its missing temperature. We can't tell which station it came from, so I didn't treat those rows as a station of their own. If you'd rather group them together and fill them from each other, tell me and I'll change it.\n\nThe project has no tests for `fill_gaps` yet, so the check above was a one-off script, not part of the test suite. I couldn't delete that script because removing files needed approval, so `chk_tmp.py` is still in the project root. You can delete it; nothing depends on it."
